s  surprisingly and deeply moved by what i  saw  number four  jaime camille enjoyed his time playing  miguel's papa and was thrilled to be  part of such a culturally rich film  camille got emotional when watching the  films just like many others but the part  that really hit him hard is when he saw  his name in the end credits because he  realized he would be part of pixar's  prestigious catalog forever it was very  special and very touching for me all  that crying however made him have to  explain to his kids why he was so  emotional crying with them is like daddy  are you sad i'm like no i'm crying out  of happiness so explaining to them is  kind of awkward  number five  the sweet and adorable mama coco was  voiced by the equally sweet and adorable  anna ofelia morgia papa was a musician  the mexican actress was 83 years old at  the time of recording her lines proving  that she is still a talented actress at  that age her career leading up to coco  is a prestigious one as she holds the  record for most nominations for best  actress for the ariel awards an award  that recognizes the best in mexican  cinema she also holds the record for  most wins for best supporting actress  for the aerial awards with such an  impressive career it's no wonder she was  chosen to voice mama coco we definitely  remembered her it's okay i'm  here who are you  number six  renee victor played miguel's music  hating abuelita she stated she loves  doing voice work because it only focuses  on the voice and not looks which meant  she could show up to the studio wearing  anything she liked a microphone doesn't  care what you look like she cited  director lee unkrich as a big help as he  guided victor through the voice acting  process so i related more to my mother  than to  uh both of my grandmothers because her  mom had a strong and energetic nature  just like the character her grandmothers  not so much no  music music  number seven  alana ubak knew she had to bring her a  game to play mama 