d her voice for tia  rosita bringing an energy to the role  that fit perfectly luna is a little  person and being cast as tia was a big  deal for her being part of coco is still  very emotional for me it validated my  20-year struggle and sacrifice as a  marginalized artist within the  entertainment industry and society as a  whole luna was able to play rosita so  well because she based her performance  off of several older women in her family  who also had nervous personalities just  like rosita and luna did an amazing job  molly needed you you're my favorite  deputy this is just one of the many  iconic lines brought to life by the  actors behind our favorite toys let's  take a look at the voices that created  these characters any other toy would  give up his moving parts just to be you  chris evans was tapped to fill the role  of buzz lightyear for the 2022 film  light year following up tim allen's  iconic role is a big task but evan seems  up to the challenge he expressed his  appreciation on twitter i can't believe  that i get to be a part of the pixar  family and work with these truly  brilliant artists director agnes mclean  said chris evans was his first and only  choice and that evans understood the  material and the character to infinity  and  there is no toy story character more  iconic than woody it was tom hanks first  voice acting gig who thrived in the role  we all knew operation playtime was a  long shot he actually recorded two  versions of the first movie as the  creators didn't like the first script so  they rewrote it and re-recorded it again  hanks explained that the recording  sessions could be stressful on his voice  and body i have driven home after a four  or five hour sometimes six hour  recording session and my diaphragm just  it hurts it aches in order to record the  more emotional scenes hanks had to  either close his eyes or turn his back  to the people in the room  tim allen's buzz lightyear voice is  easily recognizable but it's apparently  also scary as he once scared a child in  an elevator by using the voice buzz  lightyear mission log the local sheriff  and i seem to be at a huge refueling  station of some sort scaring kids aside  alan has given his all into the  character speaking on toy story 4 allen  said he got emotional watching the film  it brought up some of my own personal  stuff about loss change moving on it's  heartwarming don't worry in just a few  hours you'll be sitting around a  campfire with andy making delicious hot  schmoes the cowgirl jessie introduced in  toy story 2 was joan cusack's first  voice acting role  she stated how different it was only  using her voice to act as opposed to  live action as there were no costumes or  makeup to worry about it was kind of  cool to refocus on just your voice and  you know making something crisper clear  kuzak said that playing jessie was about  believing in yourself and what you can  do and we would say she nailed it sweet  mother of abraham lincoln toy story 4  director josh cooley found keanu reeves  when he was listening to soundbites of  potential actors he thought his voice  was perfect for the role of duke kaboom  but didn't think he was going to be able  to get reeves to voice the part however  keanu was excited about the role and  actually stood up on a table to act out  the part during a meeting with the  director duke kaboom canada's greatest  stunt man reeves didn't find the  experience too different from live  action as he said it's the same concept  of finding the right voice and tone of a  character hold on one more  oh yeah wallace sean had a great time  voicing rex for all four toy story  movies what if andy gets another  dinosaur a mean one he never lost touch  with the character even after playing  him for 24 years no matter how much time  has passed when it comes time to do it  again that dinosaur still seems to be in  me i don't have to warm up he magically  leaps into me he loves knowing that his  character can give people joy and stated  that sometimes kids recognize his voice  in public  the late comedian don rickles portrayed  mr potato head in the first three toy  story films hey look i'm picasso he was  a little hesitant to take the part at  first as he had never done voice over  work for an animated character before  luckily he changed his mind and gave mr  potato head the unique voice we know  rickles passed away before toy story 4.  but they used old recordings of his to  bring the character to life one more  time his daughter stated he would be  proud as he always said keep my name  alive let them know who i am you're not  a toy you're an accessory you're a press  with legs  right alongside mr potato head is his  wife mrs potato head voiced by the  lovely estelle harris oh you found it  this was not her first voice acting role  but it was one of her favorites as she  had a great time voicing the character  someplace dark  and dusty she described how it's a bit  difficult to know what you're recording  as they only gave her a couple pages at  a time without much context she was  skeptical about one recording in  particular where she had to make  ninja-like noises but loved it after  seeing it in the movie  [Music]  toy story 2 introduced the character of  al an avid toy collector portrayed by  wayne knight i got a pack let's see  wallet keys tickets it wasn't knight's  first time doing voice work for disney  as he had previously voiced demetrius in  hercules and tantor in tarzan knight  compared voice work to other types of  acting doing animation is interesting in  the sense that you put all your emotions  through your voice it's over the top in  a way that you don't do on stage or film  hopefully knight never had to drive all  the way to work on a saturday to voice  the toy collector  toy story 2 director john lasseter was a  big fan of kelsey grammer's portrayal of  the prospector kelsey's comic timing is  beautiful his acting it's just fantastic  grammar joked t